<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  plMail's default icon: the wax seal in its own colours, the server's
  LogoMotif::DEFAULT and what the web's icons and favicon wear. The colours are
  the "original" paint of wax-seal in tools/logo-paints.json; the tile under it
  is ic_launcher_default_background, which the build writes from the same
  entry, so this file and its tile cannot disagree with the table.

  This is the application's own `android:icon`, what the default alias wears,
  and where an unknown icon lands — a server newer than this build can name one
  that shipped after it. Repainting this file is repainting the fallback for
  every icon.

  Its geometry has a second copy, on purpose: the seal's other thirty-two
  paints are drawn at build time from app/src/launcher/motif/wax-seal.xml. The
  build compares the two stroke by stroke and fails when they stop drawing the
  same thing — LauncherIconMatrix.sameDrawing, in build-logic — so a correction
  to the seal is made in both files. The body below is that template painted
  "original", exactly as the generator writes it.

  Until v0.4.1 this was the pl mark in berry. The pl mark is now one motif
  among the others, painted from motif/pl.xml like them.

  ## The arithmetic

  The seal is drawn on the pl mark's 48 grid, scaled 1.45 and moved 19.2
  (54 - 24 × 1.45) onto the 108 canvas: larger than the pl mark's 1.2, because
  a round badge can fill more of the tile. Its scalloped edge reaches at most
  20.48 from (24, 24), 21.23 with half the 1.5 stroke, so 30.8 from the canvas
  centre: inside the radius-33 circle every mask keeps, with a little to spare.
-->
